\ api.fam — the node's API (docs/NODE.md, step 8), after sync.fam and
\ query.fam: JSON over HTTP/1.0, one request a connection, on a TCP port
\ (3738 unless configured), polled in the node's one loop with its peers.
\ Reading needs no token, nor does POST /v1/tx: it is all public (the
\ chain, the pool, a transaction to relay, as any peer could), and the
\ wallets of the OS's users read it (docs/GUI_WALLET.md).  POST /v1/token
\ carries the token, "Authorization: Bearer <64 hex digits>"; without it,
\ or with another, 401 and nothing else.  The token is made at the first
\ start (32 bytes from /dev/random, in hex) and kept in /etc/node/token,
\ mode 600; POST /v1/token makes a new one.
\
\   GET  /v1/status                      height, tip, work, peers, pool
\   GET  /v1/consensus                   the message layer's mode and relays
\                                        (cons.fam): the sets in force
\   GET  /v1/header/<height|id>[?raw]    a header, decoded (or its bytes)
\   GET  /v1/block/<height|id>[?raw]     a block kept (the last 1,008)
\   GET  /v1/outputs?from=<p>&count=<n>  outputs in position order (1,000)
\   GET  /v1/commits?from=<p>&count=<n>  name commits, the same (a reveal's)
\   GET  /v1/spent?from=<height>         positions spent, block by block
\   GET  /v1/name/<name>                 a record and its proof
\   GET  /v1/proof/output/<position>[?at=<height>]
\                                        an output's path to the state root:
\                                        the tip's, or block <height>'s (its
\                                        snapshot kept: the last 1,008), as a
\                                        proof of payment needs (apast)
\   GET  /v1/fees                        the pool's floor and dust limit, the
\                                        rates to suggest (a block, an hour,
\                                        a day; pool.fam's qsugg), economy
\   GET  /v1/mempool                     what the pool holds
\   GET  /v1/tip?after=<id>              when the tip is not <id> (30 s at most)
\   GET  /v1/events?after=<n>[&tx=<ids>][&wait=0]
\                                        the events after n, or when one comes
\                                        (30 s at most): blocks, transactions,
\                                        the node's state (below, aevents)
\   POST /v1/tx                          a transaction's bytes: pooled, relayed
\   POST /v1/token                       a new token
\
\ Digests and bytes are in hex (a digest's 32 canonical bytes; work, 32
\ bytes little-endian), numbers in decimal.  The proofs are tabminer's: an
\ output's 40 siblings, the leaf's first, the names trie's root last
\ (state_tree::Proof); a name's terminal and its siblings from it up
\ (name_trie::NameProof), with the outputs' root, which compressed with
\ the trie's makes the state root.
\
\ The API's thread (docs/NODE_ENHANCEMENTS.md, item 4).  The loop answers
\ only when it comes round: a request waited behind whatever it was doing
\ (headers saved, a batch, the pool's recheck), and behind the request
\ before it.  So the listener is a thread's (atstart: pthread, variables
\ of its own, its own buffers), which answers by itself what it can:
\ - from the store, in read transactions of its own (as of the last
\   commit, as the loop's answers were): headers, blocks, outputs,
\   commits, the spent;
\ - from what the loop publishes (the view, av: memory both see, under
\   its lock; apub, at each change and each turn of a wait): the status,
\   the tip, the events (the ring is events.fam's, read to the number
\   published), and the consensus' and the fees' answers, whole, made by
\   the loop when they change (apubs);
\ - the long polls (tip, events), waiting in its own tables, the loop
\   waking it by a byte on a pipe when the tip moves or an event comes.
\ The rest it hands to the loop (ahand: the connection and the request,
\ parsed, by a pipe the loop polls where it polled the listener), which
\ answers as before: a transaction (the pool is the loop's), a name and
\ a proof (the state's buffers), the pool's list, a new token; and a
\ header the store has not (above the tip, or genesis's).  The words
\ that answer are the same on both: on the thread the loop's variables
\ they read (myh, mytip, pact, qnum, stfd...) are its own copies, set
\ from the view before each request (aload); athr says which side.
\ Without the thread (no room for it: athon 0) the loop answers all, as
\ before.  One request at a time still, but not the loop's time.
\
\ ainit ( port -- )  the token, the listener, the thread.
\ aserve ( s -- )  s seconds of the node's loop: its peers (as nserve),
\ the API's requests, and those waiting for the tip (in sync.fam, after
\ this: api.fam comes before it, so its verifier's wait serves the API).
\ aaccept  a connection waiting, answered.

: alfd variable ;  : acfd variable ;  : atk variable ;  : arq variable ;  : arn variable ;  : ahe variable ;
: apath variable ;  : aqs variable ;  : apost variable ;  : abod variable ;  : abn variable ;  : aclen variable ;
: ao variable ;  : aop variable ;  : aoct variable ;  : aent variable ;  : aw variable ;  : aten variable ;
: aqw variable ;  : arw variable ;  : ab32 variable ;  : asib variable ;  : aauth variable ;  : apk variable ;
: awt variable ;  : ah variable ;  : ae variable ;  : ahp variable ;  : ablen variable ;  : amp variable ;
: amn variable ;  : amf variable ;  : afrom variable ;  : acnt variable ;  : an variable ;  : alast variable ;
: afromh variable ;  : alasth variable ;  : al0 variable ;  : al1 variable ;  : al2 variable ;
: aerrs variable ;  : ahh variable ;  : aend variable ;
\ What the answers read of the loop's state, set by apub just before
\ they are made: the best header's height (ahb), the peers answering
\ (apc), the newest event's number (aevn).  Not read where they live
\ (the header table, the peers' records, the ring's count) so that the
\ same words answer on a thread that has only what the loop published.
: ahb variable ;  : apc variable ;  : aevn variable ;
\ The view (av, E0 bytes from malloc): +0 its lock; +4 our height, +8
\ tip, +28 work; +48 the best header's height, +4C the peers answering;
\ +50 the pool's count, +54 bytes; +58 the activity, +5C its height;
\ +60, +64, +68 the loop's longest stall; +6C the reveal wait; +70 the
\ store; +74 the newest event; +78 the consensus' answer (malloc'd; 0:
\ none yet), +7C its length; +80, +84 the fees'; +88 set when the thread
\ has been woken and has not looked yet; +8C requests handed to the loop
\ and not yet taken; +90 the store's lock (held by the thread through a
\ request, by the loop while it makes the store afresh); +94 a request
\ that took a second or more, for the loop to tell: its ticks, +98 those
\ before its answer was sent, +9C the answer's bytes, +A0 its path (40).
\ athon: the thread runs (the loop's word); athr: this is the thread.
: av variable ;  : athon variable ;  : athr variable ;
: ahpr variable ;  : ahpw variable ;  : awpr variable ;  : awpw variable ;  : ahw variable ;  : ahr variable ;
: ahl variable ;  : ahok variable ;  : aeb variable ;  : atpe variable ;  : atpb variable ;
: apn variable ;  : apo variable ;  : apb variable ;  : apw variable ;
: apcg variable ;  : apch variable ;  : apf1 variable ;  : apf2 variable ;  : apf3 variable ;  : apf4 variable ;
: at0 variable ;  : abt variable ;  : aslt variable ;  : aslb variable ;  : asln variable ;  : asp variable ;

\ ── The response ──

: a,  aop @ c!  aop @ 1 lit + aop ! ;           \ ( c -- )
: a"  begin dup c@ ?dup while a, 1 lit + repeat drop ;   \ ( s -- )
: anum  aop @ swap snum aop ! ;                  \ ( u -- )  decimal
: ahex  ?dup if 0 lit do dup i + c@ dup 4 lit rshift nhd a, F lit and nhd a, loop then drop ;   \ ( a n -- )
: aqt  22 lit a, ;
: akey  aqt a" aqt 3A lit a, ;                  \ ( s -- )  "s":
: ahx"  aqt ahex aqt ;                           \ ( a n -- )  "hex"
: adig  20 lit ahx" ;                            \ ( a -- )  32 bytes
: acom  2C lit a, ;
: abegin  ao @ aop !  0 lit aoct ! ;             \ a body begun at ao
\ au64 ( lo hi -- )  a 64-bit number in decimal.
: au64
aw @ 1 lit w! aw @ !
aw @ 1 lit w@ 0= if aw @ @ anum else
	0 lit
	begin aw @ @ aw @ 1 lit w@ or while
		aw @ aten @ aqw @ arw @ 2 lit wdivmod  arw @ @ 30 lit + swap 1 lit +  aqw @ aw @ 2 lit wcopy
	repeat
	0 lit do a, loop
then ;

: h,  ahp @ c!  ahp @ 1 lit + ahp ! ;
: h"  begin dup c@ ?dup while h, 1 lit + repeat drop ;
: hcrlf  D lit h, A lit h, ;
\ adl: the deadline (ticks) of what the connection is doing now: its
\ header (5 s), its body (10 s), the response (10 s), so one client,
\ slow or gone, holds the node that long at most (docs/TIMING_FIXES.md).
: adl variable ;
\ awr ( a n -- )  bytes to the connection as it takes them: 4 KiB at a
\ time once it has room (poll's 4: a TCP write waits until all of it is
\ queued, and the socket holds 8 KiB), given up at adl.  (512 at a time
\ before 2026-11-13: a page of 1,000 outputs, 230 KiB, was 450 waits for
\ room, each one a turn of the scheduler's behind the worker and nodev
\ on the one hart.)
: awa variable ;  : awn variable ;
: awr
awn ! awa !
begin awn @ 0 lit >  ticks adl @ - 0< and while
	acfd @ aent @ !  4 lit aent @ 4 lit + !
	aent @ 1 lit 3B9ACA00 lit poll 0 lit > if
		acfd @ awa @ awn @ 1000 lit umin write
		dup 0 lit > if dup awa @ + awa !  awn @ swap - awn ! else drop 0 lit awn ! then
	then
repeat ;
\ asend ( status -- )  the response, its status line ("200 OK"), headers
\ and the body built at ao; the connection closed.
: asend
aop @ ao @ - ablen !  ticks abt !
arq @ ahp !  "HTTP/1.0 " h"  h"  hcrlf
aoct @ if "Content-Type: application/octet-stream" else "Content-Type: application/json" then h"  hcrlf
"Content-Length: " h"  ahp @ ablen @ snum ahp !  hcrlf hcrlf
ticks 5F5E100 lit + adl !
arq @ ahp @ arq @ - awr
ablen @ if ao @ ablen @ awr then
acfd @ close drop  0 lit acfd ! ;
\ afail ( message status -- )  {"error": message}.
: afail  swap abegin "{" a" "error" akey aqt a" aqt "}" a" asend ;
: anotf  "not found" "404 Not Found" afail ;

\ ── Between the thread and the loop ──

\ acpz ( src dst -- )  a string and its NUL; acpn ( src dst max -- )  its
\ first max bytes at most, and a NUL.
: acpz  over strlen 1 lit + bcopy ;
: acpn  2 lit pick strlen umin  2dup + 0 lit swap c!  bcopy ;
\ ahand  the request handed to the loop: its connection, the method, the
\ token's verdict, the body (the loop frees it) and the path and query,
\ in a block from malloc whose address goes down the pipe.  Eight
\ waiting there at most (a socket each, of the kernel's 32): then 503.
: ahbusy  "the node is busy" "503 Service Unavailable" afail ;
: ahand
apath @ strlen aqs @ strlen + 16 lit + malloc dup ahl !
0= if ahbusy else
	av @ lock  av @ 8C lit + @ dup 8 lit u< dup ahok ! if 1 lit + av @ 8C lit + ! else drop then  av @ unlock
	ahok @ if
		acfd @ ahl @ !  apost @ ahl @ 4 lit + !  aauth @ ahl @ 8 lit + !  abod @ ahl @ C lit + !  abn @ ahl @ 10 lit + !
		apath @ ahl @ 14 lit + acpz  aqs @  ahl @ 14 lit + apath @ strlen + 1 lit +  acpz
		ahl @ ahw @ !  ahpw @ ahw @ 4 lit write drop
		0 lit acfd !  0 lit abod !
	else ahl @ free  ahbusy then
then ;
\ aloop ( -- flag )  on the thread: the request handed to the loop.
: aloop  athr @ dup if ahand then ;
\ awkick  the thread woken (a byte on its pipe), unless it has been and
\ has not looked yet (+88: it clears that before it looks).
: awkick  av @ 88 lit + @ 0= if 1 lit av @ 88 lit + !  awpw @ "w" 1 lit write drop then ;
\ apset ( off -- )  the body at ao published at the view's off (its
\ bytes in a block of their own, the one before freed); apget ( off --
\ flag ) the answer published there as the body at ao, if there is one.
: apset
apo !  aop @ ao @ - apn !
apn @ 4 lit + malloc apb !
apb @ if ao @ apb @ apn @ 3 lit + 2 lit rshift wcopy then
av @ lock
av @ apo @ + @
apb @ av @ apo @ + !  apn @ av @ apo @ + 4 lit + !
av @ unlock
?dup if free then ;
: apget
apo !
av @ lock
av @ apo @ + @ ?dup if
	ao @  av @ apo @ + 4 lit + @ dup apn !  3 lit + 2 lit rshift  wcopy  -1 lit
else 0 lit then
av @ unlock
dup if abegin  ao @ apn @ + aop ! then ;
\ aload  on the thread: its copies of what the answers read, from the view.
: aload
av @ lock
av @ 4 lit + @ myh !  av @ 8 lit + mytip @ 8 lit wcopy  av @ 28 lit + mywork @ 8 lit wcopy
av @ 48 lit + @ ahb !  av @ 4C lit + @ apc !  av @ 50 lit + @ qnum !  av @ 54 lit + @ qbytes !
av @ 58 lit + @ pact !  av @ 5C lit + @ pacth !  av @ 60 lit + @ plg !  av @ 64 lit + @ plgh !  av @ 68 lit + @ plga !
av @ 6C lit + @ nmin !  av @ 70 lit + @ stfd !  av @ 74 lit + @ aevn !
av @ unlock ;

\ ── The request ──

\ ardy ( -- flag )  the connection readable within 2 s.
: ardy  acfd @ aent @ !  1 lit aent @ 4 lit + !  aent @ 1 lit 77359400 lit poll 0 lit > ;
\ ahend ( -- flag )  the header whole: its end, after the empty line, in ahe.
: ahend
0 lit arn @ 3 lit u> if
	arn @ 3 lit - 0 lit do
		dup 0= if
			arq @ i + dup c@ D lit = over 1 lit + c@ A lit = and
			over 2 lit + c@ D lit = and swap 3 lit + c@ A lit = and
			if drop i 4 lit + ahe ! -1 lit then
		then
	loop
then ;
\ areq ( -- ok )  the header read (8 KiB at most, 2 s a read at most, 5 s
\ in all: a byte every 1.9 s no longer holds the node for hours).
: areq
0 lit arn !  ticks 2FAF080 lit + adl !
begin
	ardy ticks adl @ - 0< and if acfd @ arq @ arn @ + 1FFF lit arn @ - read else 0 lit then
	dup 0 lit > if arn @ + arn !  ahend arn @ 1FFF lit = or else drop -1 lit then
until
arn @ 0 lit > if ahend else 0 lit then ;

\ alow ( c -- c' )  a letter in lower case.
: alow  dup 41 lit - 1A lit u< if 20 lit + then ;
\ amatch ( a name -- flag )  the bytes at a are name, in any case.
: amatch
amn ! amp !  -1 lit amf !
begin amn @ c@ while  amp @ c@ alow amn @ c@ = amf @ and amf !  amp @ 1 lit + amp !  amn @ 1 lit + amn ! repeat
amf @ ;
\ ahdr ( name -- a | 0 )  a header line's value (name in lower case, with
\ its colon), its spaces skipped; 0 if none.
: ahdr
0 lit ahh !
ahe @ 0 lit do
	ahh @ 0= if
		i 0= if -1 lit else arq @ i + 1 lit - c@ A lit = then
		if arq @ i + over amatch if arq @ i + over strlen + ahh ! then then
	then
loop drop
ahh @ dup if begin dup c@ 20 lit = while 1 lit + repeat then ;
\ ahexb ( s a n -- ok )  n bytes at a from 2n hex digits at s.
: ahd  dup 30 lit - A lit u< if 30 lit - else alow 57 lit - dup A lit - 6 lit u< 0= if drop FF lit then then ;   \ ( c -- v | FF )
: ahexb
-1 lit swap 0 lit do
	2 lit pick i 1 lit lshift + dup c@ ahd swap 1 lit + c@ ahd
	2dup or F lit u> if 2drop drop 0 lit else swap 4 lit lshift or 2 lit pick i + c! then
loop nip nip ;
\ acopy ( s d -- s' )  bytes from s to d (NUL ended) up to a space, a CR
\ or, if stop, a question mark.
: astop variable ;
: acopy
begin over c@ dup 20 lit = over D lit = or swap 3F lit = astop @ and or 0= while
	over c@ over c!  1 lit + swap 1 lit + swap
repeat
0 lit swap c! ;

\ aparse ( -- ok )  the method and path (and query: apath, aqs), the
\ token checked (aauth), the body read (Content-Length; 132 KiB at most).
: aparse
arq @ "GET " 4 lit d8= if 4 lit 0 lit else arq @ "POST " 5 lit d8= if 5 lit -1 lit else 0 lit 0 lit then then
apost !
?dup if
	arq @ +  -1 lit astop !  apath @ acopy
	dup c@ 3F lit = if 1 lit +  0 lit astop !  aqs @ acopy else 0 lit aqs @ c! then
	drop
	"authorization:" ahdr ?dup if
		dup "Bearer " 7 lit d8= if 7 lit + dup atk @ 40 lit d8= swap 40 lit + c@ D lit = and else drop 0 lit then
	else 0 lit then aauth !
	0 lit abn !  0 lit abod !
	"content-length:" ahdr ?dup if atoi else 0 lit then aclen !
	aclen @ 21000 lit u> if 0 lit else
		aclen @ if
			aclen @ malloc abod !
			arn @ ahe @ - aclen @ 2dup u> if swap then drop
			dup abn !  arq @ ahe @ + abod @ rot bcopy
			ticks 5F5E100 lit + adl !
			begin abn @ aclen @ u< if ardy ticks adl @ - 0< and else 0 lit then while
				acfd @ abod @ abn @ + aclen @ abn @ - read
				dup 0 lit > if abn @ + abn ! else drop aclen @ 1 lit + abn ! then
			repeat
			abn @ aclen @ =
		else -1 lit then
	then
else 0 lit then ;

\ apre ( s -- flag )  the path begins with s.
: apre  apath @ swap dup strlen d8= ;
\ aqv ( name -- a | 0 )  a query parameter's value (name with its "=").
: aqv
0 lit ahh !
aqs @ strlen ?dup if 0 lit do
	ahh @ 0= if
		i 0= if -1 lit else aqs @ i + 1 lit - c@ 26 lit = then
		if aqs @ i + over dup strlen d8= if aqs @ i + over strlen + ahh ! then then
	then
loop then
drop ahh @ ;
\ anarg ( name default -- n )  a numeric parameter.
: anarg  swap aqv ?dup if nip atoi then ;

\ ath ( h -- e | 0 )  on the thread: header h, at our tip or below, from
\ the store as an entry at aeb (the header, its id at CC): the id is the
\ next header's first field, or our tip's (nothing hashed here).  In the
\ caller's transaction.
: ath
dup myh @ u> if drop 0 lit else
	dup khdr aeb @ CC lit sget CC lit = if
		dup myh @ = if drop  mytip @ aeb @ CC lit + 20 lit bcopy  aeb @ else
			1 lit + khdr sbuf @ CC lit sget CC lit = if sbuf @ aeb @ CC lit + 20 lit bcopy  aeb @ else 0 lit then
		then
	else drop 0 lit then
then ;
\ atid ( s -- e | 0 )  aid on the thread: by height, or by id through
\ the store's index of ids; in a transaction of its own.
: atid
stfd @ 0 lit txbegin stx !
dup strlen 40 lit = if
	ab32 @ 20 lit ahexb if
		ab32 @ kid sbuf @ 4 lit sget 4 lit = if
			sbuf @ @ ath dup if dup CC lit + ab32 @ 20 lit d8= 0= if drop 0 lit then then
		else 0 lit then
	else 0 lit then
else
	dup c@ 30 lit - A lit u< if atoi ath else drop 0 lit then
then
stx @ txcommit drop ;
\ aid ( s -- e | 0 )  a header entry by height (decimal) or id (hex).
\ (Entries are addresses, above 2^31 in a process: 0 is none.)
: aidl
dup strlen 40 lit = if
	ab32 @ 20 lit ahexb if
		\ held or the store's, and on our best branch
		ab32 @ yfind dup if
			dup hheight phget dup if hid ab32 @ 20 lit d8= 0= if drop 0 lit then else nip then
		then
	else 0 lit then
else
	dup c@ 30 lit - A lit u< if atoi dup hbest hheight u> if drop 0 lit else phget then else drop 0 lit then
then ;
: aid  athr @ if atid else aidl then ;

\ ── The answers ──

\ ajhdr ( e -- )  a header's object.
: ajhdr
dup hhdr ah !
"{" a" "height" akey ah @ 20 lit + @ anum acom
"id" akey hid adig acom
"prev" akey ah @ adig acom
"timestamp" akey ah @ 24 lit + tamt au64 acom
"body_commitment" akey ah @ 2C lit + adig acom
"state_root" akey ah @ 4C lit + adig acom
"aux" akey ah @ 6C lit + adig acom
"mix" akey ah @ 8C lit + adig acom
"nonce" akey ah @ AC lit + adig "}" a" ;

: astatus
abegin "{" a"
"height" akey myh @ anum acom
"tip" akey mytip @ adig acom
"work" akey mywork @ adig acom
"headers" akey ahb @ anum acom
"peers" akey apc @ anum acom
"pool" akey "{" a" "count" akey qnum @ anum acom "bytes" akey qbytes @ anum "}" a" acom
"version" akey aqt "fam-node 0.1" a" aqt acom
"protocol" akey 1 lit anum acom
"activity" akey aqt  pact @ 1 lit = if "fetching" else pact @ 2 lit = if "connecting" else "idle" then then a" aqt acom
"activity_height" akey pacth @ anum acom
\ the loop's longest stall since the start (p2p.fam's pmark), in ms
"stall_ms" akey plg @ 2710 lit / anum acom "stall_height" akey plgh @ anum acom "stall_activity" akey plga @ anum acom
"reveal" akey nmin @ anum "}" a"
"200 OK" asend ;

: aheader
\ (one the thread does not find in the store, above our tip or genesis's:
\ the loop's to answer, from the headers it holds)
apath @ B lit + aid dup 0= if drop  aloop 0= if "no such header" "404 Not Found" afail then else
	abegin
	"raw" aqv if -1 lit aoct !  hhdr ao @ CC lit bcopy  ao @ CC lit + aop ! else ajhdr then
	"200 OK" asend
then ;

\ ajout ( o -- )  a block's output: commitment, memo, amount.
: ajout  "{" a" "commitment" akey dup adig acom "memo" akey dup 20 lit + 14 lit ahx" acom "amount" akey 34 lit + tamt au64 "}" a" ;
\ ajpos ( n a -- )  n five-byte positions at a, a list.
: ajpos  "[" a" swap ?dup if 0 lit do i if acom then dup i 5 lit * + pos@ au64 loop then drop "]" a" ;

: ablock
apath @ A lit + aid dup 0= if drop "no such block" "404 Not Found" afail else
	ae !
	stfd @ 0 lit txbegin stx !  ae @ hhdr 20 lit + @ ybody  stx @ txcommit drop
	over 0= if 2drop "no body kept" "404 Not Found" afail else
		abegin
		"raw" aqv if
			-1 lit aoct !  ae @ hhdr ao @ CC lit bcopy
			2dup ao @ CC lit + swap bcopy  ao @ CC lit + + aop !
		else
			2dup 0 lit bcode ! bparse
			"{" a" "header" akey ae @ ajhdr acom
			"inputs" akey bnin @ bin @ ajpos acom
			"outputs" akey "[" a" bnout @ ?dup if 0 lit do i if acom then bout @ i 3C lit * + ajout loop then "]" a" acom
			"ops" akey bnops @ anum acom
			"sweeps" akey bnsw @ bsw @ ajpos acom
			"proof_bytes" akey bnpr @ anum "}" a"
			bops @ free  drop
		then
		free  "200 OK" asend
	then
then ;

\ ajrec ( lo hi rec -- )  an output record at a position.
: ajrec
ae !  "{" a" "position" akey au64 acom
"commitment" akey ae @ adig acom
"memo" akey ae @ 20 lit + 14 lit ahx" acom
"amount" akey ae @ 20 lit + slotamt au64 acom
"height" akey ae @ 40 lit + @ anum "}" a" ;

\ a40 ( s -- lo hi )  a decimal position (40 bits), in 16-bit limbs so no
\ product overflows.
: a40
0 lit al0 !  0 lit al1 !  0 lit al2 !
begin dup c@ 30 lit - A lit u< while
	dup c@ 30 lit -  al0 @ A lit * + dup FFFF lit and al0 !  10 lit rshift
	al1 @ A lit * + dup FFFF lit and al1 !  10 lit rshift
	al2 @ A lit * + al2 !
	1 lit +
repeat drop
al0 @ al1 @ 10 lit lshift or  al2 @ ;

: aoutputs
"from=" aqv ?dup if a40 else 0 lit 0 lit then afromh ! afrom !
"count=" 64 lit anarg 3E8 lit 2dup u> if swap then drop acnt !
abegin "{" a" "outputs" akey "[" a"
afrom @ alast !  afromh @ alasth !
stfd @ 0 lit txbegin stx !
\ from the key before the first position asked for (40 bits)
afrom @ afromh @ or if
	6F lit  afrom @ 1 lit -  afrom @ if afromh @ else afromh @ 1 lit - then  kpos
else 6F lit kb @ c! 1 lit then
0 lit an !
begin
	an @ acnt @ u< if knext dup 6 lit = if drop kb2 @ c@ 6F lit = else drop 0 lit then else drop 0 lit then
while
	kb2 @ kb @ 6 lit bcopy  6 lit sbuf @ 44 lit sget drop
	an @ if acom then
	kb @ 2 lit + 4 lit be@ kb @ 1 lit + c@
	over 1 lit + dup alast !  0= if dup 1 lit + else dup then alasth !
	sbuf @ ajrec
	an @ 1 lit + an !  6 lit
repeat
stx @ txcommit drop
"]" a" acom "next" akey alast @ alasth @ au64 "}" a"
"200 OK" asend ;

\ acommits  the name commits unspent, in position order, as aoutputs:
\ each its position, its hash (the commit, canonical) and its height (a
\ wallet finds its own by hash: a reveal names the commit's position).
: acommits
"from=" aqv ?dup if a40 else 0 lit 0 lit then afromh ! afrom !
"count=" 64 lit anarg 3E8 lit 2dup u> if swap then drop acnt !
abegin "{" a" "commits" akey "[" a"
afrom @ alast !  afromh @ alasth !
stfd @ 0 lit txbegin stx !
afrom @ afromh @ or if
	63 lit  afrom @ 1 lit -  afrom @ if afromh @ else afromh @ 1 lit - then  kpos
else 63 lit kb @ c! 1 lit then
0 lit an !
begin
	an @ acnt @ u< if knext dup 6 lit = if drop kb2 @ c@ 63 lit = else drop 0 lit then else drop 0 lit then
while
	kb2 @ kb @ 6 lit bcopy  6 lit sbuf @ 24 lit sget drop
	an @ if acom then
	kb @ 2 lit + 4 lit be@ kb @ 1 lit + c@
	over 1 lit + dup alast !  0= if dup 1 lit + else dup then alasth !
	"{" a" "position" akey au64 acom "hash" akey sbuf @ adig acom "height" akey sbuf @ 20 lit + @ anum "}" a"
	an @ 1 lit + an !  6 lit
repeat
stx @ txcommit drop
"]" a" acom "next" akey alast @ alasth @ au64 "}" a"
"200 OK" asend ;

\ aspent  the positions each block kept spent: inputs, commits revealed
\ and swept.
: aspent
"from=" 0 lit anarg afrom !
myh @ 3EF lit u> if myh @ 3EF lit - afrom @ max afrom ! then
abegin "{" a" "spent" akey "[" a"  0 lit an !
stfd @ 0 lit txbegin stx !
myh @ 1 lit + afrom @ u> if
	myh @ 1 lit + afrom @ do
		i ybody over if
			2dup 0 lit bcode ! bparse
			an @ if acom then  an @ 1 lit + an !
			"{" a" "height" akey i anum acom "positions" akey "[" a"
			bnin @ ?dup if 0 lit do i if acom then bin @ i 5 lit * + pos@ au64 loop then
			bnin @ 0= 0= ahh !
			bnops @ ?dup if 0 lit do bops @ i 3 lit lshift + dup @ 2 lit = if ahh @ if acom then -1 lit ahh ! rpos pos@ au64 else drop then loop then
			bnsw @ ?dup if 0 lit do ahh @ if acom then -1 lit ahh ! bsw @ i 5 lit * + pos@ au64 loop then
			"]" a" "}" a"
			bops @ free  drop free
		else 2drop then
	loop
then
stx @ txcommit drop
"]" a" acom "height" akey myh @ anum "}" a"
"200 OK" asend ;

: aname
apath @ 9 lit + dup strlen 2dup name-ok 0= if 2drop "bad name" "400 Bad Request" afail else
	apk @ ykey
	stfd @ 0 lit txbegin stx !
	abegin "{" a" "name" akey aqt apath @ 9 lit + a" aqt acom
	"key" akey apk @ 10 lit ahx" acom
	"record" akey
	apk @ krec sbuf @ 100 lit sget 0< if "null" a" else
		"{" a" "owner" akey sbuf @ dup c@ 1 lit + + dup adig acom "value" akey dup 20 lit + adig acom "memo" akey 40 lit + adig "}" a"
	then acom
	apk @ asib @ ynproof
	"proof" akey "{" a" "terminal" akey
	1 lit = if
		"{" a" "key" akey yterm @ 4 lit + 10 lit ahx" acom "value" akey yterm @ 14 lit + ab32 @ ycanon ab32 @ adig "}" a"
	else "null" a" then acom
	"siblings" akey "[" a" ?dup if 0 lit do i if acom then asib @ i 5 lit lshift + adig loop then "]" a" "}" a" acom
	"outputs_root" akey 27 lit 0 lit ab32 @ nget  ab32 @ ab32 @ ycanon  ab32 @ adig acom
	"state_root" akey ab32 @ sroot0 ab32 @ adig acom
	"height" akey myh @ anum "}" a"
	stx @ txcommit drop
	"200 OK" asend
then ;

\ apast ( h -- )  /v1/proof/output/<position>?at=<h>: the path of the
\ output at position afrom/afromh to the state root of block h, as
\ tabminer's Chain::output_proof_at (docs/PROOFS.md: a proof of payment is
\ checked against the block that made its output): the snapshot after h
\ (serve.fam's zman and zpart, from the undo records), the part holding
\ the position or the empty subtree of the parts' lowest level, its
\ leaves (the outputs unspent then: srec and rleaf), the path inside it
\ (subtree_path), then the parts composed above it (path_from_parts: the
\ names trie's root last).  400 when block h's snapshot is not kept (the
\ last 1,008 blocks', as tabminer's undo window) or the position is 2^32
\ or more (a part's leaves are indexed from its first position, a word);
\ the output null if it was not unspent then.
: kzh variable ;  : kzhd variable ;  : kzm variable ;  : kzmn variable ;  : kzpi variable ;  : kzlv variable ;
: kzix variable ;  : kzfl variable ;  : kzfh variable ;  : kzel variable ;  : kzeh variable ;  : kzpt variable ;
: kzpn variable ;  : kzo variable ;  : kza variable ;  : kzb variable ;  : kzn variable ;  : kzi variable ;
: kzw variable ;  : kzd variable ;  : kzok variable ;  : kzsa variable ;  : kzsn variable ;  : kzsw variable ;
\ kzsib ( arr n want l -- )  the node want among arr's n (24-byte nodes:
\ an index, then a digest in Montgomery words), else level l's empty
\ subtree: as path sibling l (canonical), at asib.
: kzsib
kzw !  kzsw !  kzsn !  kzsa !
kzw @ dfl kzd !
kzsn @ ?dup if 0 lit do kzsa @ i sce + dup @ kzsw @ = if 4 lit + kzd ! else drop then loop then
kzd @ asib @ kzw @ 5 lit lshift + ycanon ;
\ kzfind  the part holding the position (kzpi, or -1), its level and
\ index (kzlv, kzix), its first position (kzfl kzfh).
: kzfind
FFFFFFFF lit kzpi !
snr @ ?dup if 0 lit do
	kzpi @ 0< if
		i 30 lit * sroots @ + dup @ swap 4 lit + @  2dup p40 kzfh ! kzfl !
		1 lit + p40 kzeh ! kzel !
		snx @ snxh @ kzel @ kzeh @ p< if snx @ kzel !  snxh @ kzeh ! then
		afrom @ afromh @ kzfl @ kzfh @ p< 0=  afrom @ afromh @ kzel @ kzeh @ p< and if i kzpi ! then
	then
loop then
kzpi @ 0< if
	E lit kzlv !  afrom @ E lit rshift afromh @ 12 lit lshift or kzix !
	kzlv @ kzix @ p40 kzfh ! kzfl !
else
	kzpi @ 30 lit * sroots @ + dup @ kzlv !  4 lit + @ kzix !
then ;
\ kzsub  the path inside the part (levels 0 to its level less one): its
\ outputs' leaves, climbed a level at a time (snap.fam's sparent), each
\ level's sibling taken on the way; the part's root then checked against
\ the manifest's (kzok 0 if it is not).
: kzsub
kzpn @ 2 lit + sce dup malloc kza !  malloc kzb !
kzpn @ ?dup if 0 lit do
	kzpt @ 4 lit + i 48 lit * + dup le@ kzfl @ - kza @ i sce + !
	srec  rb @ kza @ i sce + 4 lit + rleaf
loop then
afrom @ kzfl @ - kzi !
kzlv @ ?dup if 0 lit do
	kza @ kzpn @ kzi @ 1 lit xor i kzsib
	kza @ scb !  kzpn @ scm !  kzb @ sca !  i sparent
	kza @ kzb @ kza ! kzb !  scn @ kzpn !
	kzi @ 1 lit rshift kzi !
loop then
kzpi @ 0< 0= if
	kzpi @ 30 lit * sroots @ + 10 lit + tmpb @ dle
	kzpn @ if kza @ 4 lit + else kzlv @ dfl then tmpb @ 8 lit wcmp if 0 lit kzok ! then
then
kza @ free  kzb @ free ;
\ kzup  the path above the part: the parts composed as snap.fam's scomp
\ does, the sibling of the part's ancestor taken at each level from the
\ part's up to the outputs' half's top; then the names trie's root.
: kzup
snr @ 2 lit + sce dup malloc sca !  malloc scb !  0 lit scn !
27 lit E lit do
	i smerge
	i kzlv @ u< 0= if scb @ scm @ kzix @ i kzlv @ - rshift 1 lit xor i kzsib then
	i sparent
loop
snroot @ asib @ 4E0 lit + 20 lit bcopy
sca @ free  scb @ free ;
: apast
kzh !  -1 lit kzok !  0 lit kzpt !  0 lit kzo !
kzh @ phget dup kzhd ! 0= if "no such height" "400 Bad Request" afail else
kzh @ zman kzmn ! kzm !
kzm @ 0= if "the snapshot after that block is not kept" "400 Bad Request" afail else
kzm @ kzmn @ kzhd @ snman if kzm @ free "the snapshot after that block does not rebuild" "500 Internal Server Error" afail else
	kzfind
	\ (positions within a word: a part's leaves are indexed from its first)
	afromh @ kzfh @ or if 0 lit kzok ! then
	kzok @ if
		0 lit kzpn !
		kzpi @ 0< 0= if kzh @ kzpi @ zpart drop kzpt !  kzpt @ if kzpt @ le@ kzpn ! then then
		\ the output there then
		kzpn @ ?dup if 0 lit do
			kzpt @ 4 lit + i 48 lit * + dup le@ afrom @ =  over 4 lit + le@ afromh @ = and if kzo ! else drop then
		loop then
		kzsub  kzok @ if kzup then
	then
	kzok @ 0= if "the position is not in a part this can prove" "400 Bad Request" afail else
		abegin "{" a" "position" akey afrom @ afromh @ au64 acom
		kzo @ ?dup if
			"commitment" akey dup 8 lit + adig acom "memo" akey dup 28 lit + 14 lit ahx" acom
			"amount" akey dup 3C lit + tamt au64 acom "created" akey 44 lit + le@ anum acom
		else "commitment" akey "null" a" acom then
		"siblings" akey "[" a" 28 lit 0 lit do i if acom then asib @ i 5 lit lshift + adig loop "]" a" acom
		"state_root" akey kzhd @ 4C lit + adig acom
		"height" akey kzh @ anum "}" a"
		"200 OK" asend
	then
	kzpt @ ?dup if free then  kzm @ free
then then then ;

: aproof
apath @ 11 lit + a40 afromh ! afrom !
"at=" aqv ?dup if atoi apast else
stfd @ 0 lit txbegin stx !
afrom @ afromh @ asib @ yoproof
abegin "{" a" "position" akey afrom @ afromh @ au64 acom
afrom @ afromh @ oget if
	"commitment" akey sbuf @ adig acom "memo" akey sbuf @ 20 lit + 14 lit ahx" acom
	"amount" akey sbuf @ 20 lit + slotamt au64 acom "created" akey sbuf @ 40 lit + @ anum acom
else "commitment" akey "null" a" acom then
"siblings" akey "[" a" 28 lit 0 lit do i if acom then asib @ i 5 lit lshift + adig loop "]" a" acom
"state_root" akey ab32 @ sroot0 ab32 @ adig acom
"height" akey myh @ anum "}" a"
stx @ txcommit drop
"200 OK" asend
then ;

\ afe ( target -- )  the suggestion for a wait of target seconds: its
\ rate, and whether the pool has seen enough to estimate it (else it is
\ the minimum).
: afe  "{" a" "rate" akey dup qsugg anum acom "estimated" akey qest 0< if "false" else "true" then a" "}" a" ;
\ afees  as tabminer's `fees`: for a simple payment (2,513 bytes), the
\ rates for a block, an hour, a day; economy, the minimum, waiting at
\ most the pool's bytes over the aged reserve (179,500 a block) in blocks.
\ afeesb  its body, at ao.
: afeesb
abegin "{" a" "minimum" akey A lit anum acom "dust" akey 5CDA lit anum acom "payment_size" akey 9D1 lit anum acom
"estimates" akey "{" a" "block" akey 258 lit afe acom "hour" akey E10 lit afe acom "day" akey 15180 lit afe "}" a" acom
"economy" akey "{" a" "rate" akey A lit anum acom "blocks" akey qbytes @ 9D1 lit + 2BD2B lit + 2BD2C lit / anum "}" a" acom
"confirmations" akey qcrn @ anum
"}" a" ;
\ (on the thread: the answer the loop published, or the loop's to make)
: afees  athr @ if 80 lit apget if "200 OK" asend else ahand then else afeesb "200 OK" asend then ;

: amempool
abegin "{" a" "count" akey qnum @ anum acom "bytes" akey qbytes @ anum acom "transactions" akey "[" a"
0 lit an !
QSLOTS 0 lit do
	i qused if
		an @ if acom then  an @ 1 lit + an !
		i qslot ae !
		"{" a" "id" akey ae @ 10 lit + ab32 @ ycanon ab32 @ adig acom
		"fee" akey ae @ 8 lit + dup @ swap 4 lit + @ au64 acom "size" akey ae @ 4 lit + @ anum "}" a"
	then
loop
"]" a" "}" a"
"200 OK" asend ;

\ awhy ( code -- s )  what a pool's refusal means (qadmit's codes).
: awhy  0 lit swap - dup 15 lit u< if 2 lit lshift aerrs @ + @ else drop "refused" then ;

\ atx  the transaction offered to the pool; relayed if pooled.
: atx
abod @ 0= if "no transaction" "400 Bad Request" afail else
	abod @ abn @ qadmit
	dup 0= if
		drop  qid @ ab32 @ ycanon
		"api: tx 0 " puts ab32 @ nhex " pooled; announced to" puts
		-1 lit pnlog !  ab32 @ FFFFFFFF lit pann  0 lit pnlog !
		pnann @ 0= if " no peer (none has answered our ping yet)" puts then 0A lit putc
		abegin "{" a" "accepted" akey "true" a" acom "id" akey ab32 @ adig "}" a" "200 OK" asend
	else
		"api: tx " puts dup . 0A lit putc
		abegin "{" a" "accepted" akey "false" a" acom
		"code" akey 2D lit a, dup 0 lit swap - anum acom
		"reason" akey aqt awhy a" aqt "}" a"
		"400 Bad Request" asend
	then
then ;

\ agen  a new token: 32 random bytes in hex, written to /etc/node/token
\ (made mode 600 before it is written).
: agen
"/dev/random" 0 lit open dup ab32 @ 20 lit read drop close drop
20 lit 0 lit do
	ab32 @ i + c@  dup 4 lit rshift nhd atk @ i 1 lit lshift + c!  F lit and nhd atk @ i 1 lit lshift + 1 lit + c!
loop
0 lit atk @ 40 lit + c!
"/etc/node/token" 601 lit open
"/etc/node/token" 180 lit chmod drop
dup atk @ 40 lit write drop close drop ;

: atoken
agen
abegin "{" a" "token" akey aqt atk @ a" aqt "}" a"
"200 OK" asend ;

\ ── Events (events.fam; docs/TIMING_FIXES.md, item 15) ──
\
\ GET /v1/events?after=<n>[&tx=<id>,<id>]: the events numbered after n
\ (64 at most), at once if there are any, else when one comes or after
\ 30 s (none), as {"events": [...], "next": the last number read}; each
\ {"n", "kind", ...}: a block's ("block", "undone") "height" and "id"; a
\ transaction's ("tx") "id" and "state" (pooled; replaced, and "by";
\ evicted; mined, and "height"; conflicted; back); the node's ("status")
\ "state" (synced, syncing, "no peers"), "height" and "headers".  With
\ tx (4 at most), only those transactions' besides blocks and status.  n
\ before the oldest kept (EVN), or past the newest (the node started
\ again): {"reset": true, "next"}, the wallet reading the state afresh.
\ With wait=0, answered at once even with none.
\ AEW requests wait at most: past them, 503.
:M AEW 10 lit ;
\ a waiting request: +0 its connection, +4 until (s), +8 after, +C its
\ filter's count, +10 the ids (4 of 32 bytes)
:M AEWSZ 98 lit ;
: aew variable ;  : aeaf variable ;  : aenf variable ;  : aef variable ;  : aek variable ;
: aest variable ;  : aea variable ;  : aenx variable ;  : aep variable ;
\ aecp: the events an answer holds (64), copied out of the ring under
\ its lock; aerf: the answer is a reset.
: aecp variable ;  : aerf variable ;

\ aevst  the node's state, an event when it changes: no peers, syncing
\ (behind its best header by more than a block), synced.
: aevst
0 lit pnp @ ?dup if 0 lit do i prec 8 lit + @ if 1 lit + then loop then
0= if ENOPEERS else hbest hheight myh @ 1 lit + u> if ESYNCING else ESYNCED then then
dup aest @ = if drop else
	\ (the best header's height in the id's place, given with the event:
	\ set in the ring after, a reader could have the event without it)
	dup aest !  ab32 @ 8 lit wzero  hbest hheight ab32 @ !  EVSTAT myh @ rot ab32 @ 0 lit evput
then ;

\ aev1 ( a -- )  an event's object.
: aevbh  "height" akey aea @ 8 lit + @ anum acom "id" akey aea @ 10 lit + adig ;
: aevtxs  ( state -- s )
dup EVPOOLED = if drop "pooled" else dup EVREPL = if drop "replaced" else
dup EVEVICT = if drop "evicted" else dup EVMINED = if drop "mined" else
EVCONF = if "conflicted" else "back" then then then then then ;
: aevtx
"id" akey aea @ 10 lit + adig acom "state" akey aqt aea @ C lit + @ aevtxs a" aqt
aea @ C lit + @ EVREPL = if acom "by" akey aea @ 30 lit + adig then
aea @ C lit + @ EVMINED = if acom "height" akey aea @ 8 lit + @ anum then ;
: aevs
"state" akey aqt aea @ C lit + @ dup ESYNCED = if drop "synced" else ESYNCING = if "syncing" else "no peers" then then a" aqt acom
"height" akey aea @ 8 lit + @ anum acom "headers" akey aea @ 10 lit + @ anum ;
: aev1
aea !
"{" a" "n" akey aea @ @ anum acom "kind" akey aqt
aea @ 4 lit + @ dup EVBLK = if drop "block" a" aqt acom aevbh else
dup EVUNDO = if drop "undone" a" aqt acom aevbh else
EVTX = if "tx" a" aqt acom aevtx else "status" a" aqt acom aevs then then then
"}" a" ;
\ aem ( a -- flag )  event a wanted: not a transaction's, no filter, or
\ one of its ids.
: aem
dup 4 lit + @ EVTX = aenf @ and if
	0 lit aenf @ 0 lit do over 10 lit + aef @ i 5 lit lshift + 20 lit d8= or loop nip
else drop -1 lit then ;
\ aereset ( -- flag )  aeaf not among the numbers kept (to aevn, the
\ newest this side knows of: apub).
: aereset  aeaf @ aevn @ u>  aeaf @ 1 lit + evlow u< or ;
\ aehas ( -- flag )  a wanted event after aeaf (none looked for when
\ aeaf is not among those kept: aereset says so).
: aehas  0 lit  aereset 0= if aevn @ aeaf @ u> if aevn @ aeaf @ - 0 lit do aeaf @ i + 1 lit + evat aem or loop then then ;
\ aevans  the events after aeaf wanted (aenf, aef), 64 at most, answered:
\ copied out of the ring under its lock (evh: none being written, or
\ written over as the ring comes round), then told from the copies.
: aevans
evh @ lock
aereset dup aerf !
0= if
	0 lit aek !  aeaf @ aenx !
	aevn @ aeaf @ - ?dup if 0 lit do
		aek @ 40 lit u< if
			aeaf @ i + 1 lit + dup aenx !  evat dup aem if aecp @ aek @ EVSZ * + EVSZ bcopy  aek @ 1 lit + aek ! else drop then
		then
	loop then
then
evh @ unlock
abegin "{" a"
aerf @ if "reset" akey "true" a" acom "next" akey aevn @ anum else
	"events" akey "[" a"
	aek @ ?dup if 0 lit do i if acom then aecp @ i EVSZ * + aev1 loop then
	"]" a" acom "next" akey aenx @ anum
then
"}" a" "200 OK" asend ;
\ aevents  GET /v1/events: answered, or waiting (AEW at most).
: aevents
"after=" aqv ?dup if atoi else 0 lit then aeaf !
0 lit aenf !
"tx=" aqv ?dup if
	aep !
	begin aenf @ 4 lit u< if aep @ aef @ aenf @ 5 lit lshift + 20 lit ahexb else 0 lit then while
		aenf @ 1 lit + aenf !  aep @ 40 lit + dup c@ 2C lit = if 1 lit + then aep !
	repeat
then
\ wait=0: answered at once, events or none (a wallet's main loop asking
\ what became of its transactions, never held)
aereset aehas or  "wait=" aqv ?dup if c@ 30 lit = else 0 lit then or if aevans else
	FFFFFFFF lit AEW 0 lit do aew @ i AEWSZ * + @ 0= if drop i then loop
	dup 0< if drop "too many waiting" "503 Service Unavailable" afail else
		AEWSZ * aew @ +  acfd @ over !  secs 1E lit + over 4 lit + !  aevn @ over 8 lit + !  aenf @ over C lit + !
		aef @ swap 10 lit + 20 lit wcopy  0 lit acfd !
	then
then ;
\ aewake  the waiting requests with a wanted event, or whose time is up,
\ answered; the others' after moved past what they did not want.
: aewake
AEW 0 lit do
	aew @ i AEWSZ * + dup @ if
		dup 8 lit + @ aeaf !  dup C lit + @ aenf !  dup 10 lit + aef @ 20 lit wcopy
		aereset aehas or  secs 2 lit pick 4 lit + @ u< 0= or if
			dup @ acfd !  0 lit swap !  aevans
		else aevn @ swap 8 lit + ! then
	else drop then
loop ;

\ atipr  the tip, answered.
: atipr  abegin "{" a" "height" akey myh @ anum acom "tip" akey mytip @ adig "}" a"  "200 OK" asend ;
\ A request waiting for the tip (8 at most): its connection, until when
\ (secs: the monotonic clock, not the date), the tip it knew.
: atip
"after=" aqv ?dup if ab32 @ 20 lit ahexb if ab32 @ mytip @ 20 lit d8= else 0 lit then else 0 lit then
if
	FFFFFFFF lit 8 lit 0 lit do awt @ i 28 lit * + @ 0= if drop i then loop
	dup 0< if drop atipr else
		28 lit * awt @ +  acfd @ over !  secs 1E lit + over 4 lit + !  ab32 @ swap 8 lit + 20 lit bcopy  0 lit acfd !
	then
else atipr then ;
\ apub  what the answers read of the loop's state (ahb, apc, aevn), as
\ it is now (apubc); and, with the thread, the view written (apubv: apw
\ set if the tip moved or an event came), the thread woken then, and a
\ request of its that took a second or more told (it writes nothing to
\ the console itself: its lines would come in the middle of the loop's).
: apubc
hbest hheight ahb !
0 lit pnp @ ?dup if 0 lit do i prec 8 lit + @ if 1 lit + then loop then apc !
evn @ aevn ! ;
: apubv
av @ lock
av @ 4 lit + @ myh @ <>  av @ 8 lit + mytip @ 20 lit d8= 0= or  av @ 74 lit + @ aevn @ <> or  apw !
myh @ av @ 4 lit + !  mytip @ av @ 8 lit + 8 lit wcopy  mywork @ av @ 28 lit + 8 lit wcopy
ahb @ av @ 48 lit + !  apc @ av @ 4C lit + !  qnum @ av @ 50 lit + !  qbytes @ av @ 54 lit + !
pact @ av @ 58 lit + !  pacth @ av @ 5C lit + !  plg @ av @ 60 lit + !  plgh @ av @ 64 lit + !  plga @ av @ 68 lit + !
nmin @ av @ 6C lit + !  stfd @ av @ 70 lit + !  aevn @ av @ 74 lit + !
av @ 94 lit + @ dup aslt ! if
	av @ 98 lit + @ aslb !  av @ 9C lit + @ asln !  av @ A0 lit + asp @ 40 lit bcopy  0 lit av @ 94 lit + !
then
av @ unlock ;
: apub
awt @ if
	apubc
	athon @ if
		apubv
		apw @ if awkick then
		aslt @ vrb @ and if
			nhead "api: " puts asp @ puts " took " puts aslt @ 2710 lit / u. " ms on its thread (its answer made in " puts aslb @ 2710 lit / u.
			" ms; " puts asln @ u. " bytes written in " puts aslt @ aslb @ - 2710 lit / u. " ms)" puts 0A lit putc
		then
	then
then ;
\ atipw  the requests waiting for the tip whose tip moved, or whose time
\ is up, answered.
: atipw
8 lit 0 lit do
	awt @ i 28 lit * + dup @ if
		dup 8 lit + mytip @ 20 lit d8= 0=  secs 2 lit pick 4 lit + @ u< 0= or if
			dup @ acfd !  0 lit swap !  atipr
		else drop then
	else drop then
loop ;
\ awake  the node's state (aevst: an event when it changes), published
\ (apub); then the waiting requests answered: the events' (aewake), the
\ tip's (atipw), which with the thread are its own to answer (atmain).
\ (all of it only once ainit made the API's tables: a node's test
\ program without the API, relay_test, waits through cwait and vwait too)
: awake
awt @ if
	aevst apub
	athon @ 0= if aewake atipw then
then ;

\ acons  the message layer's mode as the chain decides it (cons.fam):
\ the tip it was made at, the epoch (height / 144), the blocks into it;
\ the set in force ("current") and, for the epoch's first five blocks,
\ the one before ("previous", else null): each its mode ("init",
\ "onion"), the winning file's hash (null: none won) and, in onion mode,
\ its relays sorted by id ({"id","address"}); and "running", what the
\ window ending at the tip decides (the next boundary's, so far).
: ajset
"{" a" "mode" akey dup @ if aqt "onion" a" aqt else aqt "init" a" aqt then acom
"hash" akey dup 8 lit + cxnz if dup 8 lit + adig else "null" a" then acom
"relays" akey "[" a"
dup 4 lit + @ ?dup if 0 lit do
	i if acom then
	dup 30 lit + i CXREL * +  "{" a" "id" akey dup adig acom "address" akey aqt 20 lit + a" aqt "}" a"
loop then
"]" a" "}" a" drop ;
\ aconsb  its body, at ao.
: aconsb
cxinit
abegin "{" a"
"height" akey cxht @ FFFFFFFF lit = if 0 lit else cxht @ then anum acom
"epoch" akey cxpinned @ if 0 lit else cxb @ 90 lit / then anum acom  "into" akey cxin @ anum acom
"current" akey cxcur @ ajset acom
"previous" akey cxprv @ 28 lit + @ if cxprv @ ajset else "null" a" then acom
"running" akey cxscr @ 28 lit + @ if cxscr @ ajset else "null" a" then
"}" a" ;
: acons  athr @ if 78 lit apget if "200 OK" asend else ahand then else aconsb "200 OK" asend then ;
\ apubs  the answers the thread gives whole, made afresh when what they
\ tell has changed: the consensus' after a scan (cons.fam's cxgen, or its
\ height: the pinned sets'), the fees' when the pool or the tip has.
\ From nstep (sync.fam), not from within a request: they are made at ao.
: apubs
athon @ if
	cxlv @ if
		cxgen @ apcg @ <>  cxht @ apch @ <> or if cxgen @ apcg !  cxht @ apch !  aconsb 78 lit apset then
	then
	qnum @ apf1 @ <>  qbytes @ apf2 @ <> or  qcrn @ apf3 @ <> or  myh @ apf4 @ <> or if
		qnum @ apf1 !  qbytes @ apf2 !  qcrn @ apf3 !  myh @ apf4 !  afeesb 80 lit apset
	then
then ;
\ astlk, astul  the store's lock, for the loop to make the store afresh
\ (main.fam): no request of the thread's is reading it then.
: astlk  athon @ if av @ 90 lit + lock then ;
: astul  athon @ if av @ 90 lit + unlock then ;

\ (aloop: on the thread, the loop's to answer)
: aroute
apost @ if
	apath @ "/v1/tx" streq if aloop 0= if atx then else
	apath @ "/v1/token" streq if aloop 0= if atoken then else anotf then then
else
	apath @ "/v1/status" streq if astatus else
	"/v1/header/" apre if aheader else
	"/v1/block/" apre if ablock else
	apath @ "/v1/outputs" streq if aoutputs else
	apath @ "/v1/commits" streq if acommits else
	apath @ "/v1/spent" streq if aspent else
	"/v1/name/" apre if aloop 0= if aname then else
	"/v1/proof/output/" apre if aloop 0= if aproof then else
	apath @ "/v1/fees" streq if afees else
	apath @ "/v1/mempool" streq if aloop 0= if amempool then else
	apath @ "/v1/tip" streq if atip else
	apath @ "/v1/events" streq if aevents else
	apath @ "/v1/consensus" streq if acons else anotf
	then then then then then then then then then then then then then
then ;

\ aone  the connection in acfd: its request read, checked, answered.
: aone
areq if aparse else 0 lit then
0= if "bad request" "400 Bad Request" afail else
	\ only a new token needs the token: the rest is public (the chain, the
	\ pool, a transaction to relay, as any peer could)
	aauth @ 0=  apost @ and  apath @ "/v1/token" streq and if abegin "401 Unauthorized" asend else aroute then
then
abod @ ?dup if free 0 lit abod ! then ;

\ ahtake  a request the thread handed over (ahand), answered here.
: ahtake
ahpr @ ahw @ 4 lit read 4 lit = if
	ahw @ @ ahr !
	av @ lock  av @ 8C lit + dup @ 1 lit - swap !  av @ unlock
	ahr @ @ acfd !  ahr @ 4 lit + @ apost !  ahr @ 8 lit + @ aauth !  ahr @ C lit + @ abod !  ahr @ 10 lit + @ abn !
	ahr @ 14 lit + apath @ acpz  ahr @ 14 lit + dup strlen + 1 lit + aqs @ acpz
	ahr @ free
	aauth @ 0=  apost @ and  apath @ "/v1/token" streq and if abegin "401 Unauthorized" asend else aroute then
	abod @ ?dup if free 0 lit abod ! then
then ;
\ aaccept  a connection to the API, if one waits (pxrdy), answered; with
\ the thread, what waits is a request it handed over.
: aaccept
pmark
pxrdy @ if
	0 lit pxrdy !  apub
	athon @ if ahtake else alfd @ accept dup 0< if drop else acfd !  aone then then
then ;

\ ── The thread ──

\ atinit ( -- ok )  on the thread: its own of every buffer its answers
\ reach (the request's, the answer's 2.1 MiB, the numbers', the tables of
\ those waiting, the events copied, the store's keys and values, our tip
\ and work, a header's entry), and room left for its stack.
: atinit
-1 lit athr !
2000 lit alloc arq !  2000 lit alloc apath !  2000 lit alloc aqs !  220000 lit alloc ao !
10 lit alloc aent !  8 lit alloc aw !  8 lit alloc aten !  8 lit alloc aqw !  8 lit alloc arw !
20 lit alloc ab32 !  10 lit alloc ahw !
140 lit alloc awt !  AEW AEWSZ * alloc aew !  80 lit alloc aef !  40 lit EVSZ * alloc aecp !
100 lit alloc kb !  100 lit alloc kb2 !  400 lit alloc sbuf !
20 lit alloc mytip !  20 lit alloc mywork !  120 lit alloc aeb !  20 lit alloc atpe !  20 lit alloc atpb !
ao @ 0= 0=  atpb @ 0= 0= and  8000 lit alloc 0= 0= and
dup if
	awt @ 50 lit wzero  aew @ AEW AEWSZ * 2 lit rshift wzero
	A lit aten @ !  0 lit aten @ 4 lit + !  0 lit acfd !  0 lit abod !
then ;
\ atone  the connection in acfd answered: the view taken (aload), the
\ store's lock held through it; one that took a second or more left in
\ the view for the loop to tell.
: atone
ticks at0 !  0 lit abt !  0 lit ablen !
aload
av @ 90 lit + lock  aone  av @ 90 lit + unlock
ticks at0 @ - dup 989680 lit u< if drop else
	av @ lock
	av @ 94 lit + !  abt @ if abt @ at0 @ - else 0 lit then av @ 98 lit + !  ablen @ av @ 9C lit + !
	apath @ av @ A0 lit + 3F lit acpn
	av @ unlock
then ;
\ atmain  the thread's loop: a connection, the loop's byte (the tip
\ moved, an event came) or a second (the waiting requests' time); the
\ view taken, those waiting answered if they can be, a connection
\ answered.
: atmain
begin
	alfd @ atpe @ !  1 lit atpe @ 4 lit + !  awpr @ atpe @ 8 lit + !  1 lit atpe @ C lit + !
	atpe @ 2 lit 3B9ACA00 lit poll drop
	atpe @ C lit + @ 10 lit rshift if awpr @ atpb @ 10 lit read drop then
	\ (cleared before the view is taken: a change after it wakes us again)
	0 lit av @ 88 lit + !
	aload  aewake atipw
	atpe @ 4 lit + @ 10 lit rshift if alfd @ accept dup 0< if drop else acfd !  atone then then
0 lit until ;
\ atstart  the view, the two pipes (the requests handed over: ahpr the
\ loop's end; the wake: awpw the loop's), the view written, the thread
\ started: its first word down the requests' pipe says whether it had
\ its buffers (athon).  Its block: 2.25 MiB of the node's own heap.
: atstart
0 lit athon !  0 lit athr !
E0 lit malloc av !  10 lit alloc ahw !  44 lit alloc asp !  10 lit alloc ahl !  10 lit alloc ahr !
av @ if
	av @ 38 lit wzero
	ahl @ pipe 0< 0=  ahr @ pipe 0< 0= and if
		ahl @ @ ahpr !  ahl @ 4 lit + @ ahpw !  ahr @ @ awpr !  ahr @ 4 lit + @ awpw !
		FFFFFFFF lit apcg !  FFFFFFFF lit apf1 !
		apubc apubv
		ptcode[ drop
			atinit  dup ahw @ !  ahpw @ ahw @ 4 lit write drop
			if atmain then
		]tcode
		0 lit 240000 lit pthread 0< 0= if
			ahpr @ ahw @ 4 lit read 4 lit = if ahw @ @ if -1 lit athon ! then then
		then
	then
then ;

: ainit  ( port -- )
2000 lit alloc arq !  2000 lit alloc apath !  2000 lit alloc aqs !
10 lit alloc aent !  8 lit alloc aw !  8 lit alloc aten !  8 lit alloc aqw !  8 lit alloc arw !
20 lit alloc ab32 !  F00 lit alloc asib !  44 lit alloc atk !  10 lit alloc apk !
140 lit alloc dup awt ! 50 lit wzero
AEW AEWSZ * alloc dup aew !  AEW AEWSZ * 2 lit rshift wzero  80 lit alloc aef !
40 lit EVSZ * alloc aecp !  evn drop
A lit aten @ !  0 lit aten @ 4 lit + !  0 lit acfd !  0 lit abod !
54 lit alloc aerrs !
"does not decode" aerrs @ 4 lit + !  "no inputs" aerrs @ 8 lit + !  "malformed" aerrs @ C lit + !
"too large" aerrs @ 10 lit + !  "an output below the dust limit" aerrs @ 14 lit + !
"outputs exceed inputs" aerrs @ 18 lit + !  "fee below the minimum" aerrs @ 1C lit + !
"invalid signature" aerrs @ 20 lit + !  "spends an output that is not unspent" aerrs @ 24 lit + !
"already in the pool" aerrs @ 28 lit + !  "a name or commit already claimed" aerrs @ 2C lit + !
"a replacement short of its fee" aerrs @ 30 lit + !  "the pool is full" aerrs @ 34 lit + !
"no commit for the reveal" aerrs @ 38 lit + !  "the commit expired" aerrs @ 3C lit + !
"the name is registered" aerrs @ 40 lit + !  "the name is not registered" aerrs @ 44 lit + !
"not the owner's update" aerrs @ 48 lit + !  "a policy input's leaf not satisfied" aerrs @ 4C lit + !
"too many signatures for a segment" aerrs @ 50 lit + !
\ the token: kept, or made
"/etc" mkdir drop  "/etc/node" mkdir drop
"/etc/node/token" 0 lit open dup 0< if drop agen else
	dup atk @ 40 lit read 40 lit = if close drop 0 lit atk @ 40 lit + c! else close drop agen then
then
\ the listener
2 lit socket alfd !
alfd @ 1 lit 0 lit 3 lit pick net drop  drop
alfd @ 3 lit 0 lit 0 lit net drop
\ the thread, if it can be had: the loop then polls what it hands over,
\ and makes its answers (small: the largest the pool's list) in 256 KiB;
\ without it, the listener and the 2.1 MiB a page of outputs takes
atstart
athon @ if 40000 lit alloc ao !  ahpr @ pxfd ! else 220000 lit alloc ao !  alfd @ pxfd ! then ;
